  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "point-condition",
   "text": "x has support {a}. Its image is inside C({a})."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "nesting-condition",
   "text": "C({a}) is disjoint from C({a,b}): the required containment fails."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Select a face, then drag x. The condition must hold for every face and every point."
  },
  {
   "tag": "summary",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Why? / The definition"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "A carrier assigns regions, not individual output points. For each nonempty face σ, C(σ) is a subspace of Y. Smaller faces must receive smaller allowed regions: τ ⊆ σ ⇒ C(τ) ⊆ C(σ)."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "A continuous map f: |Δ| → Y is carried when f(⟨σ⟩) ⊆ C(σ) for every nonempty face σ. Neither the carrier regions nor the images have to equal Y."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "case-explanation",
   "text": "Since {a} ⊆ {a,b}, a carrier must satisfy C({a}) ⊆ C({a,b}). Here these two regions are disjoint. No map can satisfy both constraints at a: f(a) would have to lie in both. Having nonempty, contractible regions is not sufficient without nesting."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Source: Björner, Nerves, fibers and homotopy groups, p. 89 (Carrier Lemma)."
  },
  {
   "tag": "a",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Source: Björner, Nerves, fibers and homotopy groups, p. 89 (Carrier Lemma)."
  }
